'''Eikthyr''' is the first [[Creatures#Bosses|boss]]. He appears as an abnormally large stag with iron chains wrapped around his electrified red antlers.

== Summoning ==
[[File:EikthyrAltar.png|left|thumb|Eikthyr's Forsaken Altar.|200x200px|alt=]]
Eikthyr's [[Forsaken Altars|Forsaken Altar]] is located in the [[Meadows]]. To the left of his [[Sacrificial Stones|Sacrificial Stone]] is a small glowing [[Runestone]] called a [[Runestone#Vegvisir|Vegvisir]]; interacting with it will add his closest summoning location on the map.

He is summoned by placing two {{Item Link|Deer Trophy}} in his Forsaken altar in the Meadows. Like all bosses, Eikthyr can be summoned as many times as desired, provided the required materials are met.

== Attacks and abilities ==
{{For|strategies for defeating Eikthyr|Boss strategies#Eikthyr}}
Eikthyr has three types of attacks in addition to an environmental aura that forces darkness and removes raining.

=== Antler ===
A swiping melee attack with his antlers (20 [[Damage types#Pierce|Pierce]], 1000 Tier 0 [[Damage types#Chop|Chop]] and 1000 Tier 0 [[Damage types#Pickaxe|Pickaxe]] damage). This attack features a 5-second cooldown and can be used when a player is within 4 meters. It has a range of 4.5 meters and hits in a horizontal arc spanning 25 degrees.

=== Charge ===
A ranged beam attack that fans out horizontally 45 degrees and extends 20 meters out (15 [[Damage types#Lightning|Lightning]] damage). On contact, the beam will inflict the [[Lightning (effect)|Lightning]] status. This has a 25-second cooldown and Eikthyr can attempt to use this ability when a player is within 15 meters.

=== Stomp ===
A 10-meter radius area-of-effect attack that expands outward from the center and inflicts the [[Lightning (effect)|Lightning]] status (15 [[Damage types#Lightning|Lightning]] damage). This attack has a 40-second cooldown. He can use this ability when a player is within 6 meters.

== Aftermath ==
Defeating Eikthyr allows the player to craft the first pickaxe to begin mining ore to create metal tools, weapons, and armor. 

=== Drops ===
{{CreatureDrops|stars=0}}

=== Forsaken power ===
Mounting Eikthyr’s trophy upon his respective stone will allow the player to claim his Forsaken Power. This ability will grant the player and nearby allies the following effects for 300 seconds:

* Run stamina usage: -60%
* Jump stamina usage: -60%
* Swim stamina usage: -60%

=== Events ===
Defeating Eikthyr affects the following [[events]] for that world:

* Disables: "Eikthyr rallies the creatures of the forest."
* Enables: "The forest is moving..." (if [[The Elder]] hasn't been defeated)

=== Creature spawning ===
Defeating Eikthyr unlocks [[Greydwarf]]s to spawn in the Meadows at night. They can only have 0 stars.

